  "coordinator_analysis": "The strengthened multi-hop decomposition instruction was validated on 3 distinct failed cases across 3 domains: Billboard chart trivia (trial_002, score 1), musician classification (trial_004, score 1), and film/Walk of Fame trivia (trial_005, static PASS score 1). The basic version (trial_003) failed because the Actor guessed John Candy without verifying his Academy Award count. The strengthened version added 'Do not rely on internal knowledge — search to verify each claim about each entity' which forced the Actor to search for the correct four-time nominee (Annette Bening, star year 2006) via sequential sub-queries. Trial_001 (Simpsons bowling) confirmed that decomposition alone cannot overcome a genuine corpus gap — the mechanism correctly decomposes but cannot fabricate absent evidence. The mechanism generalizes across different multi-hop patterns: entity-to-attribute chain, two-entity independent verification, and song-to-property chain. Execution cost increases modestly (1-2 extra tool calls, ~2-3k additional tokens) but is justified by the correctness improvement.\n\nLimitations: (1) Only 3 of 15 failure cases were tested as validation; (2) Not tested on chemistry/geography domains from the failure pool; (3) One case (trial_001) showed the mechanism cannot compensate for absent corpus evidence.",
